             "type": "TEXT",
             "x": 0.0,
             "y": 34.0,
             "w": 343.0,
             "h": 412.0,
             "strokeWeight": 0.4000000059604645,
             "strokeAlign": "CENTER",
             "fills": [
              {
               "type": "SOLID",
               "color": "#000000"
              }
             ],
             "text": {
              "characters": "A panic attack is a sudden episode of intense fear or discomfort that usually peaks within minutes. During an attack, the body reacts as if it is facing a serious threat, triggering strong physical and emotional symptoms.  Common symptoms may include:\nRapid heartbeat or chest pain\nShortness of breath\nDizziness or feeling faint\nSweating or shaking\nNausea or stomach discomfort\nTingling sensations\nFeeling detached from reality\nFear of losing control or dying\nBecause these symptoms can feel severe, some people mistake panic attacks for heart attacks or other medical emergencies.",
              "fontSize": 16.0,
              "font": {
               "family": "Roboto",
               "style": "Regular",
               "postscript": "Roboto-Regular"
              },
              "lineHeight": {
               "value": 22.0,
