             "y": 34.0,
             "w": 343.0,
             "h": 346.0,
             "strokeWeight": 0.4000000059604645,
             "strokeAlign": "CENTER",
             "fills": [
              {
               "type": "SOLID",
               "color": "#000000"
              }
             ],
             "text": {
              "characters": "Panic disorder occurs when panic attacks happen repeatedly and create ongoing fear about when the next attack might occur. Over time, this fear can affect daily routines, work, social activities, and relationships.  People with panic disorder may begin to:\nAvoid crowded places or unfamiliar situations\nStay away from activities that trigger anxiety\nConstantly worry about their physical health\nFeel anxious even when there is no immediate danger\nWithout support, panic disorder can gradually reduce a person’s confidence and quality of life.",
              "fontSize": 16.0,
              "font": {
               "family": "Roboto",
               "style": "Regular",
               "postscript": "Roboto-Regular"
              },
              "lineHeight": {
               "value": 22.0,
